# The Art of Teaching the Art of Applying Mathematics

**Authors:** Lighthill, M. J.

## Abstract
This article (the 1971 Presidential Address to the Mathematical Association of U. K.) makes a plea that college teachers of mathematics should be better aware of the applications of mathematics in other subjects. As an example, the author describes the use of differential equations to solve certain vibrational problems in mechanical engineering. (MM)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ044842

